{0 The workero CLI}

[workero build] turns an OCaml executable with [(modes wasm)] into a
directory that Wrangler can serve and deploy.

{1 Usage}

{@sh[
workero build <dir>/<name> [--out <dir>]
]}

Run it from the root of the dune project. [<dir>/<name>] names the executable:
[workero build src/main] builds [src/main.ml]. [--out] sets the output
directory. The default is [_worker].

{1 What it does}

+ Runs [dune build --profile release <dir>/<name>.bc.wasm.js].
+ Removes the [*.wasm.assets] directories that earlier runs left in the output
  directory, so a second run leaves one set of [.wasm] files.
+ Copies the wasm_of_ocaml loader ([<name>.bc.wasm.js]) and its
  [<name>.bc.wasm.assets] directory into the output directory.
+ Writes [load-wasm.js], which loads the precompiled wasm modules in workerd.
+ Writes [index.js], the worker entry point. It imports every [.wasm] file and
  exports the handlers that the program registered with {!Workero.serve} and
  {!Workero.scheduled}.

It prints [workero: wrote <dir> (<n> wasm file(s))]. On an error it prints
[workero: <reason>] to stderr and exits with code 1.

{1 Errors}

[workero build] exits with code 1 and prints [workero: <reason>] to stderr when:

- the arguments do not match the usage,
- [dune build] fails,
- dune does not produce the loader or the [.wasm.assets] directory (the
  executable lacks [(modes wasm)], or the path is wrong),
- the program uses OCaml functions that have no wasm implementation. The
  message is [workero: <name> uses functions with no wasm implementation:
  <list>]. They would fail at run time. Provide a wasm implementation with
  [(wasm_of_ocaml (wasm_files ...))], or drop the library that needs them.

The check also works for programs built with [--pretty] in [wasm_of_ocaml]
[flags].

{1 With Wrangler}

Point [main] at the generated [index.js] and run [workero build] as the build
command, so [wrangler dev] and [wrangler deploy] rebuild the worker:

{@toml[
main = "_worker/index.js"

[build]
command = "workero build src/main"
watch_dir = "src"
]}

wasm_of_ocaml needs [wasm-opt] from binaryen 119 or later on [PATH]. The npm
package [binaryen] provides it.
